# Crisis-Grid: Emergency Resource Allocator System — Project Summary

---

## Executive Overview

**Crisis-Grid** is an emergency response & healthcare logistics platform designed to optimize emergency ambulance routing and ICU bed allocation in real-time. The system processes field location signals, patient vital signs, and natural-language dispatch text to match incoming ambulances with the optimal receiving hospital across major Tamil Nadu medical centers (Chennai, Coimbatore, Madurai, Trichy).

---

## Key Capabilities Built

1. **Smart Emergency Allocation Algorithm**: Calculates optimal hospital receiving units based on distance, travel ETA, bed availability ratios, patient severity, and specialized care matching (ICU, Cath Lab, Burn Unit, Neuro ICU, Trauma).
2. **AI Emergency Triage Engine**: Automatically analyzes patient symptoms and vitals (SpO2, Pulse, Blood Pressure, Temperature) to assign clinical severity (Levels 1–5) and infer required specialties.
3. **NLP Dispatch Intake**: Parses dispatch audio/text transcripts to extract GPS coordinates, location keywords, urgency scores, and medical specialty requirements.
4. **Predictive Capacity & Bed Forecasting**: Projects hospital bed availability for 1-hour, 3-hour, and 6-hour windows using discharge velocity models and capacity strain risk alerts.
5. **Real-Time Command Map**: Visualizes hospital network status, live ambulance markers, and active routing polyline paths on an interactive OpenStreetMap view.
6. **Real-Time WebSocket Synchronization**: Broadcasts capacity updates and allocations live across all connected clients.

